# * ==== DATABASE ====
# * There's two ways of set-up the database: internal and external. Choose ONLY one.
# ? Internal: the docker compose construct and defined the DATABASE_URL
# ?     automatically by the env vars below. Uncomment if you want to
# ?     override the defaults.

# POSTGRES_USER=olim
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD=a-very-strong-pwd
# POSTGRES_DB=olim
# # Define the following var when you want to expose the postgres outside docker
# # internal host.
# POSTGRES_EXPOSE_PORT=

# ? External: a external database is set-up and has provided a URL, just define
# ?     it below.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://olim:a-very-strong-pwd@localhost:5432/olim

# * ==== CELERY (pipeline execution) ====
# ? The worker runs pipeline blocks as background tasks. Redis is the broker and
# ?     result backend; docker compose points these at its `redis` service by
# ?     default. Uncomment to override (e.g. an external Redis, or running the
# ?     worker on the host against localhost).
# CELERY_BROKER_URL=redis://localhost:6379/0
# CELERY_RESULT_BACKEND=redis://localhost:6379/1

# * ==== ARTIFACTS ====
# ? Where a block writes its output for the next block to read. Defaults to the
# ?     `artifacts` docker volume mounted at /artifacts. Set a writable local path
# ?     when running the worker outside docker.
# ARTIFACT_ROOT=/artifacts
